.DS_Store
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/


# pixi materialises environments here. The lockfile is tracked; this is not --
# it is several hundred MB of solved packages, one copy per environment.
.pixi/

# Simulation trajectories are data a run's record names, not records, and they
# are not tracked: text trajectories run to tens of MB each, a deleted file
# frees nothing once it is in git history, and the person deletes them by hand
# when space is needed. The record that says what was written --
# trajectory_meta.json -- is tracked, hence the exception below. plan.md
# section 4.6 on trajectories.
simulation_agent/runs/*/trajectory*
!simulation_agent/runs/*/trajectory_meta.json

# A usage tracker on the microscope computer writes its ledger into .agent/
# at whatever directory a session starts in. It is not a record of this
# repository; SKIP_DIRS in contracts/validate.py carries the same name, and
# check 79 requires the two to agree (2026-10-03).
.agent/

# The runtime's idle status (plan.md 15.1 item 3): one file the runtime writes after
# every run and every "check now", volatile and never a record -- records stay in
# runs/<id>/. Named uniquely so SKIP_DIRS can carry it by name, as check 79 requires,
# without skipping any other directory; SKIP_DIRS took it first at d549cc42
# (manager-microscope-20261003-1, 2026-10-22).
.runtime_status/
